\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  My soul remember the troubles
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj that Jesus had and died for you
\par If you are so hungry for Him,
\par eat His flesh and then drink His blood.
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj If my Jesus loves me so well,
\par it gives a great joy to my heart;
\par He takes my pains to be His own
\par and gives to me all His goodness.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  I know my Saviour already,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 and I have in Him my comfort,
\par He teaches me all the right paths
\par to the golden street of Heaven.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par As long as I have my Saviour,
\par I have no joy in anything,
\par and have chosen Him as my friend,
\par I give Him all praise for Mercy.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  But I can with many misses
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 draw so near to the Lord's table;
\par If I partake in this supper
\par deeply I will be satisfied;
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par It's because I could see so clear
\par He made this so great covenant,
\par and had rescued me from deaths' grips
\par and He gave His life for my sake.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. These broken bread that I see now,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 I shall partake and give Him thanks;
\par It is part of my Saviour's flesh
\par through which came life everlasting.
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6   Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par He was wounded just for my sake
\par \pard\sl190\slmult0      crucified Him on His own cross
\par      and was laid in that great stone tomb
\par       and resurrected in glory.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.   This wine that have received blessings,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 We will drink it with thanksgiving;
\par And it is the blood of Jesus
\par that He shed for me on the cross.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par If my soul is thirsty for Him
\par and I only need His presence,
\par He will this wine made my witness
\par that my sins shall be forgiven.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.  O, my Saviour, I'm so wretched,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 but your grace is bounteous for me;
\par You have redeemed me from my sins,
\par and you saved me from all evil.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par And  so Lord, cleanse me from my heart,
\par dwell in me your Holy Spirit.
\par Let my spirit, soul and body
\par have your grace and eternal life.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7.  O, my Saviour and my lover,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 What again then should I look for?
\par What is so greater than your love
\par to us than your eternal life?
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par If I have Him as my Saviour,
\par there is nothing so to worry;
\par not afraid in death nor in hell
\par my Saviour is my protector.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

